# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) before running `npm run sync:youtube`.
#
# Optional: without it the sync falls back to the channel's public RSS feed,
# which needs no key but only covers the ~15 most recent uploads and carries no
# duration or view counts.
#
# How to get one:
#   1. console.cloud.google.com -> create (or pick) a project
#   2. APIs & Services -> Library -> enable "YouTube Data API v3"
#   3. APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key
#
# Restrict the key to "YouTube Data API v3" and keep it out of any client-side
# bundle: it belongs to the build environment only.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# Accounts + cloud data (Supabase Auth + Postgres) ---------------------------
# Set BOTH to enable accounts and synced data. There is no local-only account
# fallback: without them the login screen reports that Supabase is not
# configured (the console warning names exactly which var is missing).
#
# Get them from your Supabase project: Settings -> API.
#   Project URL        -> VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#   publishable / anon -> VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# The publishable/anon key is safe in client code: it only grants what the Row
# Level Security policies allow. Never put the service_role / secret key here.
#
# Also run supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql once in the SQL editor, and disable
# Authentication -> Email -> "Confirm email" while testing if you want sign-up
# to log in immediately (see README -> Accounts).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
